<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experimental setup</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the detailed statistics of the training datasets used in our experiments, along with the implementation details.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Data statistics and implementation details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.1 Data statistics and implementation details ‣ Appendix A Experimental setup ‣ Beyond Reasoning Gains: Mitigating General Capabilities Forgetting in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports the full statistics of the training corpora used in our experiments.
For LLaVA-OneVision-OCR, we extract OCR-focused subsets from the official LLaVA-OneVision release  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>:IIIT5K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mishra et al., 2012</a>)</cite>, HME100K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">hme, 2021</a>)</cite>, IAM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Marti &amp; Bunke, 2002</a>)</cite>, TextCaps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sidorov et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, and TextOCR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib89" title="" class="ltx_ref">Singh et al., 2021</a>)</cite> alongside release-provided synthetic/curated subsets (rendered_text, k12_printing, chrome_writing). Those images are resized so that the longer side is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 512</annotation></semantics></math> px while preserving aspect ratio to mitigate out-of-memory errors without altering task semantics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A1.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Data statistics of each data source.<span id="A1.T3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We present the original volume of data (# samples).
</span></span></figcaption>
